      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-12-15T19:26:42.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"arenson9\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/48/1900_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> arenson9:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>Silverleaf wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Interesting that in the base game review he says he'd have preferred minis to the tokens, and then in the expansion review he complains that the minis aren't easy to distinguish and that unless you're going to paint the tokens are better. Make up your mind Tom! ;)\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nActually, I completely agree &nbsp;with that sentiment.Minis are more fun than tokens, but the unpainted minis are problematic such that the (beautiful!) tokens are better, even though they're just tokens.I had been starting to fear that my money spent on the painted tokens was a waste, but after playing with the painted minis at the tournament, I am _SO_ happy I could afford to purchase them.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The pre-painted mini quality is fantastic. It is very high on my list of purchases once they hit the online store</p>",
